# Build context is the repo root (`docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .`), so this
# file must live HERE, not in docker/.
#
# Allow-list style: exclude everything, then re-add only what the Dockerfile
# COPYs. Keeping the context tiny also stops docs/YAML edits from busting the
# build cache.
*

# runtime code (engine + use cases + infra) and host/build tooling, baked to /app/*
!scripts
!scripts/**
!engine
!engine/**
!infra
!infra/**
!usecases
!usecases/**

# the retry wrapper used by every network step (COPY docker/retry.sh ...).
# Without this the build fails instantly with "failed to compute cache key:
# not found" -- the whole point of the allow-list is that new COPYs must be
# added here too.
!certs
!certs/**
!vendor
!vendor/**
!docker
docker/*
!docker/retry.sh
# compile-only probe for the FlashInfer/CCCL toolchain check (Dockerfile step 5c).
# Kept as a real file because escaping a multi-line .cu through
# Dockerfile -> /bin/sh -> printf mangled the #include directives.
!docker/cccl_probe.cu
